1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
The Clover Kingdom.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In this place where magic is everything,

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
there lives one boy who was born without it.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
His name is Asta.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
His strength and determination helped him become a magic knight.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
And despite the many challenges he faces,

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
he aims for the top and refuses to give up.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Rich or poor, royalty or commoner,

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Asta believes anyone can shine.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
His mission is to prove that to the whole world

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
and to become the next Wizard King.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Those flowers are for me?

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Yes. I hope you like them.

14
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Don't just give them away.

15
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
It's fine. You're my hero, so I want to give you a gift.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Dad?

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Zora, come over here for a sec.

18
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
I should be on my way now.

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
What happened?

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
They smell really nice, don't you think?

21
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
I've always been partial to this fragrance.

22
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Yeah, I know.

23
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
I know.

24
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

25
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,000
I feel like I'm so happy

27
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,140
But the l goalまだ decides exactly what

28
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:26,020
I'm like.

29
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:28,000
Help me as well as...

30
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Wow, wow, wow, wow, wow...

31
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,260
Yeah, yeah

32
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:38,500
Yeah, yeah

33
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:45,700
強く風吹く世界の果てで

34
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:51,240
僕らは今日も目を閉じる夢を見る飽きもせず

35
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:56,700
今は小さく儚い希望も

36
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:02,060
いつか時代を変えてゆく光になると信じて

37
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:06,720
背負うべきものなど何一つないさ

38
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:09,560
全て抱きしめてゆく

39
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:14,020
例えばそれが痛みだとしても

40
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:18,700
叶うなら君と共に

41
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:26,140
この声がこの喉が振り切れるほど今叫ぶよ

42
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:30,520
未来は自分で切り開くんだって

43
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:35,180
止めるとなく溢れ出る情熱のままさ

44
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:37,180
歩き出そう

45
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:42,180
Tooth is my dream

46
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:50,180
Yeah, like I have time for crap like that

47
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:53,000
I don't need to train with them

48
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,780
I didn't join the Black Bulls to make new friends and play around

49
00:02:56,780 --> 00:03:05,020
Taking a little solo trip to get some practice in was obviously the best choice

50
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:07,100
It'd probably slow me down

51
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:11,740
But at some point, I guess I should change my ways

52
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:15,360
Right?

53
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:16,640
Dad?

54
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:16,680
Dad?

55
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:26,480
I doubt anyone from back home left these here

56
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:31,400
Since Dad was the first commoner to become a magic knight

57
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,100
People used to call him the bride of Tulsa village

58
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:46,400
But that's all in the past now

59
00:03:46,400 --> 00:04:05,060
Man

60
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:09,220
He did that with no grimoire?

61
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:11,000
This kid's got potential

62
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,840
Well, good luck with that

63
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:20,760
Who's there?

64
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,480
Oops, look at that

65
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:26,520
Wow, Kaito, that flame magic of yours is really incredible

66
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:29,460
I can't believe you managed to hit the target from all the way over there

67
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:32,820
Yeah, I can't wait for you to take the magic knight's entrance exam

68
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:35,220
Now isn't the time for flattery

69
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:38,140
A rich kid, all the way out here

70
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:41,120
Family must be getting away for the summer

71
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,100
What's wrong?

72
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,500
You look mad

73
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,480
Say sorry!

74
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,680
Did you just tell Kaito to apologize?

75
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,460
You better watch your mouth

76
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:53,420
Relax, he's just a baby who doesn't have his grimoire yet

77
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:55,660
And he's a commoner too, no less

78
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:59,080
Here

79
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,900
That should fix it

80
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,060
Let's go

81
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:05,120
I may be a commoner

82
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:08,220
But when I turn 15

83
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,000
And I get my own grimoire

84
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,620
Don't tell me

85
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,700
You think you're going to become a magic knight

86
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:14,260
Exactly

87
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,040
In fact, I know I will

88
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:19,880
Sorry, but I think you'll find that's impossible for the lower class

89
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:20,860
You're wrong

90
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,440
It wouldn't be the first time a peasant did that

91
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:24,620
Is that true?

92
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,400
Oh yes, and they've made quite a splash

93
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:31,200
Then I guess there had to have been some special reason why they were accepted

94
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,240
They probably had dirt on somebody important

95
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:36,240
I know Zara Ideale didn't get in that way

96
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:40,960
Who's Zara Ideale?

97
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,780
Huh, beats me

98
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,000
What squad?

99
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,360
The Purple Orcas

100
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:49,160
Ha, isn't that the one that all those terrible rumors were about?

101
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:52,360
The one whose captain had to be replaced because of some huge scandal?

102
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,840
Zara still did amazing things

103
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,280
Yeah, I've never heard of him

104
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:59,580
What kind of amazing things does he do?

105
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,400
What, you can't even name one?

106
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,860
Well, he's dead now

107
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,440
He died on a mission

108
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:10,940
See what I mean?

109
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:15,580
You peasants need to know your place and stay in your little villages until you die

110
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,080
Shut up

111
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:23,240
What kind of spell was that?

112
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:25,960
Make sure he pays

113
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,960
Right, we'll teach him

114
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:31,840
Dumb commoner

115
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:33,580
Apologize to Kaito

116
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,820
No way

117
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,160
Do it now

118
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,260
I'm not in the wrong here

119
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:39,960
I see

120
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:45,360
All right, that's enough

121
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:48,820
Yeah, and who are you?

122
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,920
It's staying!

123
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:54,520
Hold it!

124
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:05,260
Did I just do that?

125
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:07,880
You haven't seen the last of us, commoner

126
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:10,720
Man, you're dense

127
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:15,340
You can't go picking fights when you're up against three guys

128
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:20,440
Since you don't have a grimoire yet, those punks would have chewed you up and spit you out

129
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:24,480
I know you're just a kid, but you gotta have at least some common sense, right?

130
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:30,440
Although, that stuff you said about Zara being a great magic knight

131
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,880
Well, you weren't wrong about that

132
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:36,260
Ina? What's going on out here?

133
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:38,560
Oh, dad

134
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:42,280
Son, why do you look so upset?

135
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:43,840
Are you hurt?

136
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,600
You don't need to worry

137
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,720
I'm fine

138
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,480
He helped me out

139
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:51,720
Oh, then I'm sorry for the trouble, sir

140
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:58,180
Ina, what happened?

141
00:07:58,180 --> 00:07:59,300
Be honest

142
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,780
You know you can talk to me about anything, son

143
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:08,620
You peasants need to know your place and stay in your little villages until you die

144
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:12,280
Why was I born into a poor family?

145
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:18,400
If I wasn't a commoner, my magic would be more powerful, and life wouldn't be so hard

146
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,560
It's not fair

147
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,380
Why did I have to be your son?

148
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:21,820
What?

149
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:25,140
No, don't

150
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:27,860
He's absolutely right

151
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:28,640
Huh?

152
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:33,980
If our family wasn't in this sorry state, Ina wouldn't have to help me with my work

153
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:37,880
And then I could give him more time to improve his skills with magic

154
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,420
You see?

155
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:41,440
I'm an awful father

156
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:46,440
Hey, let go of me

157
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,440
Where are you going?

158
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:54,920
That young man, he's kind of familiar

159
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:59,720
You can't just carry me off

160
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,380
Awesome mask guy

161
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:01,700
Huh?

162
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:03,180
Call me that

163
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:03,960
What?

164
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,620
Don't tell me what to do

165
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:07,180
And I'll call you shrimp

166
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:09,240
No, snot-nosed shrimp

167
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,920
I'm not a snot-nosed shrimp

168
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,380
Back to what we were talking about

169
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:14,820
It's true

170
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:18,500
Zara was a great magic knight who happened to be a peasant

171
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,820
Yeah, and?

172
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:22,220
He must have had something I don't have, right?

173
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,420
That's not what I'm saying

174
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:27,200
Zara never complained about growing up the way he did

175
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:29,020
As a matter of fact

176
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:32,040
I don't remember him ever saying a harsh word about anybody

177
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:33,360
Wait a sec, mask guy

178
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,300
You knew him?

179
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,060
Awesome mask guy, kid

180
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:38,820
And yeah, I knew him

181
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:39,500
But you're right

182
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,940
There were a lot of things about him that were nothing like you

183
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:46,580
It's fine, okay?

184
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,180
I know that I'm aiming too high

185
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:53,040
Aiming too high?

186
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:54,140
That's what I said

187
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,420
You're a commoner

188
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,760
There's no way you could be one of the magic knights

189
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:02,520
Well, I may have failed the magic knights entrance exam more times than I can remember

190
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:06,380
But I don't think I've set my sights on something that's unachievable

191
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:07,060
Huh?

192
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,060
Zara

193
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:11,480
Zara, I'm always telling you I'll join the magic knights, aren't I?

194
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:12,760
Well, son

195
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:16,340
That's because I honestly believe that it'll happen one day

196
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:24,580
You told those brats you'd get into the magic knights

197
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:25,700
So you heard

198
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,180
What, is that a problem?

199
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:29,300
Nah, I don't care what you do

200
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,080
My thing is

201
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,940
If you're able to say something like that with a straight face

202
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:36,120
It must mean you really think you can do it

203
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:39,120
And if that's the case

204
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,940
Then you're not aiming too high

205
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,600
Zara used to talk like that too

206
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:47,480
Maybe I really do believe that it'll happen

207
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:51,700
Let me give you a bit of advice, not no shrimp

208
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,880
I said to stop calling me that

209
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,460
What the heck?

210
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,280
Is that doll supposed to be you?

211
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,880
This guy is Zara the super mage

212
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,800
The mysterious herald of justice

213
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,880
I'm not a toddler

214
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:08,140
He may talk a lot of smack, but he's a good man

215
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,440
He fights evil from the shadows

216
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:12,500
What a lame backstory

217
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,460
And are you seriously into dolls?

218
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,060
How old are you?

219
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:19,020
Zara was the son of a peasant just like you are

220
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:21,340
But he was never impressed by nobles or royalty

221
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:25,460
Because deep down he knew there was something he could do that they couldn't

222
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:27,260
Stop ignoring me

223
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:31,440
Wait, did you say Zara had something the rich people didn't?

224
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:34,920
Hmm, now I wonder what that could be

225
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:36,100
How the hell would I know?

226
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,340
Guess you don't

227
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:40,180
But if you want to be a magic knight one day

228
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:43,180
Then you better figure it out

229
00:11:43,180 --> 00:12:08,560
Zara was the son of a peasant just like you are

230
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:10,900
But he was never impressed by nobles or royalty

231
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:14,880
Because deep down he knew there was something he could do that they couldn't

232
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:17,100
I wonder what that could be

233
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,820
Let's take a lunch break

234
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:22,380
I can handle this afternoon's workload

235
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:25,600
So feel free to go practice your magic if you want

236
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:45,720
So we meet again

237
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:49,040
I graciously let you off the hook yesterday

238
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:52,480
But now you'll pay for what you did

239
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,200
Look, commoner

240
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,980
Ever seen one of these before?

241
00:12:58,460 --> 00:12:59,360
No way

242
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:01,460
Now that I have this

243
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:03,700
Idiot

244
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,120
Kids shouldn't mess with magic items

245
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,040
I just want an apology

246
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,320
Is that so difficult?

247
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,720
Now, get down on your knees and grovel

248
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:13,160
I didn't do anything

249
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:13,900
All right

250
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:15,300
One more chance then

251
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:18,320
Apologize to me or suffer the consequences

252
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:22,800
You dumbass

253
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:39,740
That's strike too

254
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:42,220
Go play with something more your speed

255
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:48,740
You're really powerful, huh?

256
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:51,340
Almost like a magic knight

257
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:52,920
Eh, maybe

258
00:13:52,920 --> 00:14:13,780
Ina

259
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:18,180
There you are

260
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,800
You little thief

261
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:22,420
Can I help you, sir?

262
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,720
Hey, what are you doing to my son?

263
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:29,960
See this?

264
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,560
Isn't that a magic item?

265
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:36,320
Your little delinquent snuck into my private villa and purloined it!

266
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:37,440
What? No!

267
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:40,380
Don't lie to me, boy

268
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:43,960
If you didn't steal it, then what's it doing in this pathetic hovel?

269
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:47,020
Look, your son's obviously the one who stole it

270
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:50,080
I just picked it up after he dropped it on the ground

271
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,520
Tell me, Kaito

272
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,200
Is that true?

273
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,780
Don't let yourself be fooled

274
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:57,380
